      "message": "[warning] Line 350: 🟡 `loadEarlierMessages()` determines exhaustion via `all { it.messageId in knownIds }`, but many legacy interactions can have `messageId \u003d\u003d null`. Since `null` is a single set member, newly loaded null-id messages are treated as already known, so paging may stop after one fetch even when older history exists. Use a stable per-row identity (`messageId ?: \"legacy:${id}\"`) or compare list growth/new tail identity instead of raw nullable `messageId` membership.",
